{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_04_array_iteration_methods_02_callbacks_holes_and_async_three_arg_callback", "label": "Iteration callback (element, index, array)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/04-array-iteration-methods/02-callbacks-holes-and-async.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every iteration method passes three arguments. Passing a named function whose later params mean something misfires."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_04_array_iteration_methods_02_callbacks_holes_and_async_map_parseint", "label": "map(parseInt) radix bug", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/04-array-iteration-methods/02-callbacks-holes-and-async.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\"].map(parseInt) is [1, NaN, NaN] because index arrives as parseInt radix."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_04_array_iteration_methods_02_callbacks_holes_and_async_find_visits_holes", "label": "find visits holes; forEach skips them", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/04-array-iteration-methods/02-callbacks-holes-and-async.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "MDN: find is invoked for every index, treating holes as undefined. forEach skips empty slots. Same sparse array: 7 visits vs 3."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_04_array_iteration_methods_02_callbacks_holes_and_async_mutate_while_iterating", "label": "Mutating an array while iterating", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/04-array-iteration-methods/02-callbacks-holes-and-async.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Range is fixed before the first callback. Appended elements are not visited; removals cause skips. Build a new array."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_04_array_iteration_methods_02_callbacks_holes_and_async_async_foreach", "label": "async forEach discards promises", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/04-array-iteration-methods/02-callbacks-holes-and-async.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "forEach expects a synchronous function and does not wait for promises. MDN example prints 0 instead of 14. filter(async) filters nothing because every promise is truthy."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_04_array_iteration_methods_02_callbacks_holes_and_async_sequential_vs_concurrent", "label": "for...of await vs Promise.all(map)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/04-array-iteration-methods/02-callbacks-holes-and-async.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "for...of + await is sequential. Promise.all over map is concurrent. Pick by independence and load."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_04_array_iteration_methods_02_callbacks_holes_and_async_page", "label": "04.2 \u00b7 Callbacks, holes and async", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-5-built-in-library/04-array-iteration-methods/02-callbacks-holes-and-async.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_5_built_in_library_04_array_iteration_methods_02_callbacks_holes_and_async_page", "target": "docs_javascript_page